Upgrade procedure for openresolv

Source: https://github.com/NetworkConfiguration/openresolv/releases/download/vVERSION/openresolv-VERSION.tar.xz
	Check openresolv-VERSION.tar.xz.asc with gpg and Roy Marples'
	key A785ED2755955D9E93EA59F6597F97EA9AD45549 (roy@marples.name),
	and compare the sha256 sum with the one in the release notes.
	Releases before 3.17.0 have no release tarball; the GitHub tag
	archive (archive/refs/tags/vVERSION.tar.gz) was used for 3.9.2.

The vendor branch is vendor/openresolv, in-tree prefix contrib/openresolv,
tag vendor/openresolv/VERSION.  The vendor branch carries the release minus
the files listed in MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist (just .gitignore), so that its tree
matches contrib/openresolv.  Its first commit is the 3.9.2 import that was
already in the tree; master was joined to it with a merge that changed no
files (the same way as vendor/zlib), later updates use "git subtree merge".

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and verify the tarball and extract it into a new directory.
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/openresolv, contrib/openresolv).
   Stage with "git add -A -f", remove the Xlist files first and check that
   the committed tree is identical to the tarball minus the Xlist files.
3. Merge with "git subtree merge -P contrib/openresolv vendor/openresolv".
4. Update the build glue in sbin/resolvconf/Makefile if configure or the
   upstream Makefile gained new @VARIABLE@ substitutions
   (grep -ho '@[A-Z_]*@' contrib/openresolv/*.in | sort -u), new
   subscribers (the FILES list, only libc, dnsmasq, named, pdnsd,
   pdns_recursor and unbound are installed) or new manual pages.
5. Build sbin/resolvconf, install it into a DESTDIR and run it with a
   resolvconf.conf that points resolv_conf and the state directory at
   temporary files (resolvconf -a, -d, -u, -l, -i).

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  None.  The libc.in change that 3.9.2 carried here (writing resolv.conf
  with echo instead of printf %s) was dropped in the 3.17.4 update: it only
  added a trailing blank line and upstream now has resolv_conf_mv handling.

Local build glue (sbin/resolvconf/Makefile, not part of contrib):

  - sed substitutions for SYSCONFDIR, LIBEXECDIR, VARDIR, RESTARTCMD, RCDIR,
    SBINDIR and STATUSARG (onestatus, for service(8)).
  - RESTARTCMD uses "service $1 onestatus && service $1 restart".
  - " vpn " in the dynamic_order list of resolvconf is rewritten to
    " ng[0-9]* vpn " so that ng(4) devices are ordered like VPNs.

Notes:
  - Not installed: avahi-daemon, mdnsd, resolvectl and systemd-resolved
    subscribers (added upstream after 3.9.2).
  - FreeBSD carries one change after 3.17.4 in resolvconf.in (strip a
    leading dot in process_domain(), FreeBSD aad298c8f9ca); MidnightBSD
    does not carry it.
